    {
      "id": "da32c10e9aae426b",
      "role": "C",
      "mission": {
        "base_commit": "ac6798963b13b6b7073cb45c8adc7ebcfb1a6406",
        "delegation_parent": "R/C",
        "depth": 1,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "Pairing along the smaller matrix dimension reduces the scan work, while a reusable per-thread frequency table and parallel work sharing reduce hashing and serial execution costs without assumptions about matrix values.",
        "id": "da32c10e9aae426b",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "C",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/main.cpp"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Compress each row/column band along the shorter dimension, transposing tall matrices so the scan remains contiguous; complexity is O(min(m,n)^2 * max(m,n)).",
            "Replace per-band unordered_map operations with a bounded, power-of-two open-addressed table using signed 64-bit keys/counts and generation stamps for reuse.",
            "Work-share independent band starts with dynamic scheduling and a 64-bit reduction; use a generic work threshold to avoid parallel overhead on small inputs."
          ]
        },
        "tree_id": "e1:C",
        "trial_id": "01M51RPTEM6CJRPBVBFYHZCEFA",
