        "depth": 2,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "Orient the matrix so the smaller dimension forms the paired strips, reducing strip work for rectangular inputs. For each strip, contiguous independent element-wise accumulator updates are explicitly SIMD-enabled, while the dependent prefix-frequency scan remains sequential.",
        "id": "5afc2b0f77d3462e",
        "ordinal": 2,
        "parent_id": "93bf143823a7441d",
        "role": "B",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/main.cpp"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Choose the smaller matrix dimension as the paired-strip dimension; transpose the input when necessary so the scanned dimension is contiguous.",
            "Replace the 2D row-prefix table with incremental strip accumulators, adding one contiguous oriented row per strip extension.",
            "Apply OpenMP SIMD only to independent accumulator elements; keep the loop-carried prefix sum and frequency-map scan sequential.",
            "Parallelize independent strip starts with per-thread scratch state and answer reduction, retaining a work-based sequential fallback."
          ]
        },
