        "depth": 1,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "Replacing dynamic dispatch with cyclic static scheduling for the triangular band-start loop should reduce OpenMP scheduling overhead while keeping work balanced: band-start costs decline smoothly with the start index, so static,1 distributes similarly sized total work among workers. The reusable frequency table, contiguous band scans, and work threshold preserve correctness and avoid parallel overhead on small inputs.",
        "id": "26f1ebe86c514c54",
        "ordinal": 2,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "G",
        "source_commits": [
          "b0c7a4e462d912da6b38634cb4b4628599fdefda",
          "f40b2862c4e6fcf260cfdc50434eaae71b7093df"
